## The 2 constraint modules

FIN and OPS are different from the rest. Every other module tells the system what to
do. These 2 tell it **what the brand is capable of doing**.

- **FIN is the cash constraint.** A brand cannot act on a recommendation that ties up
  money it does not have for 90 days.
- **OPS is the capacity constraint.** A brand with 1 founder and no designer cannot
  execute a 40-creative-a-month plan.

Both become preconditions on plays. A system that ignores them produces a to-do list
nobody will ever action, which is worse than producing nothing.

