## Capture budget

15 to 25 minutes per source you keep. Most of that is screening, not capture.
Open it, look for specific numbers, sequences and conditions in the first 2 minutes,
close it if there are none. Expect to keep 1 in 4.

The test: would a good model already say this? "Write unique title tags" is noise.
"Collection pages competing for the same query lose roughly 8 to 25% of impressions
to each other, and consolidation takes 60 days to show" is the whole point.
Collect the number, the threshold, the sequence, the exception, the condition.

WLD is the one exception. There, capture the mechanism and the cost ceiling even
when there are no numbers, because there will never be numbers until somebody runs
it.

Roughly 440 sources at a full library. Never collect toward that total. Collect
toward the current phase. Per-module volumes are in `_MODULE-GUIDE.md`.
